    "narrative": "With the Austin Waves pushing for category gains today, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** anchors the lineup as our premier offensive weapon against Gore. His efficiency score of 72.41 reflects a high-ceiling matchup, bolstered significantly by a 7% dynamic platoon advantage against the lefty and prime protection in the #3 hole. Alongside him, we are maximizing our speed-focused strategy, prioritizing **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who remain locked into the primary rotation due to their sprint speed profiles\u2014our primary hedge against the volatility of the AVG and SB categories in a tight Roto race. \n\nThe most difficult decision on today's docket was relegating **Nasim Nunez** to the bench. Despite his elite speed profile, his score of 39.78 fell just shy of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" While his switch-hitting ability usually adds utility, the matchup against S\u00e1nchez\u2014a pitcher boasting a sub-3.00 xERA\u2014proved too daunting, further hampered by a 2% penalty for facing a high-efficiency catcher and a lack of positive BvP history. We are playing it cautious today; with **Luis Robert Jr.** still sidelined on the IL and **Gunnar Henderson** enjoying an off-day, we cannot afford to burn game caps on high-risk, low-efficiency scenarios. Keep a close eye on **Drake Baldwin** and **Heliot Ramos** as potential late-game pivots should our primary starters fail to manufacture early runs, but for now, the objective is to maintain efficiency while we await the return of our core power-speed anchors like **Kyle Tucker** and **Josh Lowe**.",
